<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- APNs environment for push notifications.

	     This file is used by the **Release** configuration only. Debug and
	     Profile both point at RunnerDebug.entitlements, which deliberately has
	     no aps-environment at all so a free personal team can still sign to a
	     device. An earlier version of this comment said "development" was
	     correct for debug builds via flutter run — it is not, because those
	     builds never read this file.

	     So the value here has to serve two things Flutter gives one config to:

	       flutter run --release on a device   development-signed -> "development"
	       Archive for TestFlight / App Store  distribution-signed -> "production"

	     It is left at "development" so device testing works, because that is
	     what happens more often and its failure is loud. The other failure is
	     silent: an App Store build carrying "development" registers against the
	     APNs sandbox and production pushes simply never arrive, with nothing in
	     the app to say why.

	     **Before archiving for TestFlight or the App Store, set this to
	     "production".** If that proves easy to forget, the durable fix is a
	     separate RunnerRelease.entitlements wired to the Archive action rather
	     than a note in a file. -->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
